{
  "question": "What did Apollo astronauts actually do on the lunar surface, and what did they bring back?",
  "plan": {
    "sub_questions": [
      "What surface activities and field tasks did Apollo astronauts perform during lunar EVAs?",
      "What kinds of samples and other material did they collect and return to Earth?",
      "What equipment, experiments and vehicles did they deploy, use, or leave on the Moon?"
    ],
    "phrasings": [
      "What did Apollo astronauts actually do on the lunar surface, and what did they bring back?",
      "Apollo astronauts performed extravehicular activities on the lunar surface conducting geology fieldwork and exploration.",
      "Astronauts collected rock and soil samples and returned them to Earth for laboratory analysis.",
      "Astronauts deployed scientific experiments and emplaced the Apollo Lunar Surface Experiments Package and other instrumentation.",
      "Astronauts used the Lunar Module for landing and ascent and wore portable life\u2011support suits during surface operations.",
      "On later Apollo missions astronauts used the Lunar Roving Vehicle to extend surface traverses and carry equipment.",
      "Returned manifest included rock and core samples, film and photographic records, and experiment hardware recovered from the lunar surface."
    ],
    "visual_phrasings": [
      "Astronauts in bulky extravehicular suits walking on the gray dusty lunar surface carrying sample bags, scoops and rock cores.",
      "Crew members deploying instruments, planting a flag, and assembling/placing experiment packages on the regolith.",
      "Close-ups of bagged rock and core samples, camera film magazines, and equipment being loaded into the Lunar Module or rover."
    ],
    "needs_chronology": true,
    "rationale": "I split the query into surface activities, returned materials, and equipment/experiments to match how NASA narration separates EVA tasks, sample return, and hardware deployment over successive Apollo missions."
  },
  "answer": {
    "answer": "The archive shows Apollo crew descending to and walking on the lunar surface during EVAs (for example Buzz Aldrin\u2019s descent) [2].  While on the surface they collected and photographed lunar rocks and soil\u2014material explicitly shown in the archive as lunar rocks [5].  The record also shows that at least some missions left one crewmember in lunar orbit while others went down to the surface (Michael Collins stayed in orbit while others landed) [4].  Taken together, these clips imply a mission pattern in which teammates descended to conduct surface EVAs, collect samples, and return physical lunar material to Earth while others remained in orbit [2][5][4].",
    "citations": [
      2,
      5,
      4,
      9
    ],
    "chronology": [
      {
        "citations": [
          2,
          5,
          4
        ],
        "claim": "Video-era Apollo clips show surface EVAs (descent and walks) and sample collection, and also note that a crewmember could remain in lunar orbit while others landed",
        "era": 1969
      },
      {
        "citations": [
          9
        ],
        "claim": "Later Apollo-era material (Apollo 17) emphasizes field geology and systematic sampling by astronaut-geologists",
        "era": 1972
      }
    ],
    "caveats": "Dates are taken from the archive era labels (some items are marked as era_axis: video/published in the metadata, e.g. [2]) rather than being independently verified by on-screen content; the clips do not establish totals of samples returned, a complete inventory of tools or experiments, or the full procedures used on every mission."
  },
